**Figure 1.** Pilot running estimate of pi (4 x hits/samples, cumulative) against cumulative sample count (log axis), 55 checkpoints ~10 s apart, up to n = 1.759e9 (final 3.141554, 95% CI [3.141477, 3.141631], see `results/estimate.json`). Red line: true pi. Grey: expected pi ± 1.96 sigma_n envelope, sigma_n = 4 sqrt(q(1-q)/n), q = pi/4. Top panel y-axis is zoomed, so the first checkpoint (n = 1e5) is shown but the envelope is clipped there. Bottom: error in units of sigma_n; all checkpoints lie within ±1.96. Points are cumulative and therefore strongly correlated, not independent.
